@startuml lab_onboarding
' Time-ordered view: what actually happens when vfd2 is plugged into cellA.
' Render:  plantuml lab_onboarding.puml
title Leaf onboarding flow — from "vfd2" to a routed, named device

autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false

participant "vfd2\n(dhclient -6)" as DEV
participant "cellA radvd" as RA
participant "cellA Kea DHCPv6" as KEA
participant "cellA Kea-D2\n(DDNS writer)" as D2
participant "cellA BIND9\n(authoritative)" as DNS
participant "line3 Kea\n(PD upstream)" as LINE

== Address block already delegated (cascaded PD) ==
LINE -> KEA : (earlier) IA_PD -> cellA gets fd12:3456:789a:0301::/64

== Leaf appears on the wire ==
DEV -> DEV : form fe80::, run DAD (RFC 4862)
RA  -> DEV : Router Advertisement\nManaged=1  => "use DHCPv6"
DEV -> KEA : SOLICIT (IA_NA, Option 39 FQDN="vfd2", ORO: DNS/domain)
KEA -> KEA : pick addr from pool ::100-::1ff\nappend ddns-qualifying-suffix
KEA -> DEV : REPLY  addr fd12:3456:789a:0301::1xx\n+ domain cellA.line3.plant.acme.internal
KEA -> D2  : NameChangeRequest (add AAAA + PTR for vfd2)
D2  -> DNS : DNS UPDATE (RFC 2136) signed with TSIG (RFC 8945)
DNS -> DNS : write AAAA in forward zone\nwrite PTR in ip6.arpa reverse zone
D2  --> KEA : ack

== Result ==
note over DEV, DNS
  vfd2.cellA.line3.plant.acme.internal  <->  fd12:3456:789a:0301::1xx
  (forward and reverse now answer each other)
end note
@enduml
